course: dictionary
lesson: 4590
title: Words that announce
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A herald is a messenger who tells people important news before it arrives. Long ago, a herald was an official for a king or queen. He carried messages and read out announcements loudly so that everyone could hear.
explain: The word can also mean a sign. «The herald of spring» is something that shows spring is coming, like snowdrops pushing through the cold ground. Look at the words around herald to decide whether it means a person or a sign.
explain: As a verb, herald means to be a sign that something is about to happen, or to announce something loudly. Snowdrops herald spring: they show us it is on its way. Check by swapping in show or announce. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: A herald is a messenger or announcer who makes important news known.
fact: «The White Rabbit is the herald, the officer who reads announcements.» In Alice in Wonderland, he blows a trumpet and reads out the charge at the trial.
fact: «Herald» can also mean a sign that something is coming, as in «the herald of spring».
fact: In history, heralds announced news for kings and queens, and they also organised coats of arms.
fact: Many newspapers have herald in their name, such as «The Herald», because a newspaper announces news to its readers.
exercise: «The White Rabbit is the herald, the officer who reads announcements.» What is a herald in this sentence? | A kind of trumpet | A rabbit who lives in a burrow | *An officer who reads announcements | A sign that winter is coming
exercise: «Snowdrops herald the coming of spring.» What does herald mean here? | To cover the ground with frost | To pick flowers | To fall asleep under the snow | *To be a sign that something is about to happen
exercise: In the carol «Hark! the herald angels sing», the angels are called heralds of Jesus' birth. What are heralds in this carol? | *Messengers who announce important news | Stars in the night sky | Musicians in a choir | Kings who travel far
test: The newspaper «The Herald» is named after a herald. What does that suggest? | It sells flowers and plants | *It announces news to its readers | It tells stories about the past only | It is written only for kings and queens
test: «The trumpet blasts herald the start of the trial.» What does herald mean? | To paint a picture | *To announce that something is about to begin | To hide from danger | To forget what happened
exam: «The bright sun heralded a warm summer.» What does heralded mean? | *Showed that something was about to come | Wrote about | Melted away | Hid from
